* **Zero-Trust Isolation:** Enforcing strict boundary checks between local subsystem layers to prevent unauthorized external tampering or data extraction.
* **Real-Time Integrity Verification:** Continuous assertion checks ensuring operational state consistency against the hardened OS posture.

## Scrambled Logic (Simulated FHE)
Scrambled Logic implements simulated Fully Homomorphic Encryption (FHE) principles across all input and output pipelines:
* **Payload Obfuscation:** Ensures that if any transport or storage layer is intercepted, the communication payload remains completely uninterpretable outside of the secure local session instance.
